issues.suggested_fix:
Unify the delete API to use the person's UUID consistently. The least-disruptive fix is to change the solution's PersonService.deletePerson signature to accept a UUID (matching the problem and template) and remove by id. For example:

public void deletePerson(UUID personId) {
    this.persons.removeIf(p -> p.getId().equals(personId));
}

Ensure all callers (e.g., PersonResource.deletePerson) pass the UUID. Alternatively, if you prefer service-layer deletion by object, update PersonResource to resolve a Person object before calling the service — but the first option aligns best with the exercise description and template and reduces student confusion.
